1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
In this video, I will introduce the functions of the virtual model for you.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,000
In the 2025 version, we can use the slide to easily adjust the shape of the male and female virtual models.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:25,000
To demonstrate this function, we add a female virtual model of FV2.1 and open the virtual model editor.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:35,000
In the shape of the virtual model size, you will see a new hip part, which includes two adjustable parameters, waistline and size.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
In the default situation, both are set to 50%.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
You can create various hip shapes by changing these values.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The way the slide is operated is the same as the operation of adjusting the chest shape.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
It can be easily controlled by dragging the slide.

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
You can also make more accurate adjustments by inputting values directly on the right side.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:03,000
If you want to reset all the changes to default, you can press the reset button in the upper right corner.

11
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Turn the view to the back to observe.

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Now let's see how the hip shape changes when adjusting each parameter.

13
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The first parameter is the waistline.

14
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The waistline can adjust the natural waistline between the hip and thigh sides.

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Slide the slide to the left to reduce the waistline value.

16
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Note that when moving the slide for the first time, it may pop up a message window.

17
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
If you choose not to display, the next time you move the slide, the window will not appear.

18
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Press OK to confirm, then move the slide to the left.

19
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
As the value decreases, you will see that the curve on both sides of the hip is more curved.

20
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Slide the slide to the right to move the slide, which can fill the volume on both sides of the hip, and thus form a rounder hip shape.

21
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Next, let's create a more flat or more curved hip by adjusting the second parameter size.

22
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Let's turn to the side view to observe.

23
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:08,000
You will see that there are two options at the bottom of the slide.

24
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
If you slide a slide, you can create a more flat hip shape.

25
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Slide a slide can increase the size of the upper part of the hip and improve the appearance of the hip.

26
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
This function is also used in male virtual models.

27
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:27,000
First, let's add a male virtual model in the mv2.1 version.

28
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
You will find the hip in the same position.

29
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
The type and O-line and volume parameters are the same as female virtual models due to the same operation process.

30
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,000
You can directly adjust the value and adjust the hip according to your needs.

31
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Please note that adjusting these hip parameters will not affect the size, value, or measurement of the hip or lower hip.

32
00:02:50,000 --> 00:03:00,000
By using the new function in the virtual model editor, you can easily create various hip shapes.

33
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
In the previous version, we have to use the third-party software to name each pair of shoes or earrings correctly,

34
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
in order to correctly define the shoes in the colo.

35
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:14,000
In the latest version, the customized symmetry configuration will become more convenient.

36
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Next, we will use shoes as an example.

37
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
First, open a virtual model.

38
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Then, click on the virtual model in the main menu bar.

39
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Select the customized configuration.

40
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:28,000
In the customized configuration, find the configuration type and select shoes.

41
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Then you can choose flat shoes or high heels.

42
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Here, use high heels to demonstrate.

43
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
Next, click on the file plus icon.

44
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Insert the file containing two shoes at the same time.

45
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:44,000
After this update, we also support the file with the input OBJ format.

46
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
After the update, colo can automatically identify each shoe.

47
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:52,000
There is no need to name it by left or right.

48
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,000
In addition, in the new version, you can directly select two shoes.

49
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Right-click and select shoes.

50
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,000
You can see that the shoes will be displayed in red.

51
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:05,000
It's just the shoes you chose.

52
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:10,000
If you set it wrong, you can right-click again and select cancel settings as shoes.

53
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,000
This step is only applicable to high heels.

54
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Because it needs to automatically raise the virtual model's heel to adapt the heel when loading.

55
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Next, we will save the shoes.

56
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:29,000
So, next time, you can directly use the saved configuration file.

57
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:34,000
I hope these functions can help you optimize the workflow.

58
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Make the process of customizing the matching configuration more convenient.

59
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Next, I will introduce you to the 2025.0 version.

60
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Another workflow that can greatly simplify the workflow.

61
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Now you can see that the virtual model currently has a side position.

62
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:57,000
In the previous version, if you want to do the mirror effect of the current position, you must modify the position from the beginning.

63
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:03,000
But in the new version, you only need to right-click on the virtual model and then select the flip position option.

64
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
This will immediately convert the virtual model into a flip position.

65
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:09,000
And the costume will also be simulated accordingly.

66
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:13,000
This function allows you to try various positions and easily flip them.

67
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Therefore, it is more free to test the effect of different angles when simulated.

68
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:24,000
In the new version, the virtual model editor also has another important update.

69
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
You can create and edit.

70
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,000
The chest of the female virtual model is the same size as the cup.

71
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Let's see how to edit it.

72
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Open the virtual model editor.

73
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Under the virtual model size option card.

74
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:39,000
In the width, select the chest.

75
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Now you can set the detailed information.

76
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Activate the cup size option.

77
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:49,000
After activating, you can set the standard size of the chest.

78
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
You can change the number of sizes.

79
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
The smallest value is 3.

80
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
The largest value is 6.

81
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:00,000
In addition, you can also change the name and value of each cup size.

82
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:04,000
This value indicates the difference between the chest and the lower chest.

83
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:11,000
If you want to reset it to default, you can click reset.

84
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,000
After setting up.

85
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
You can exit the detailed information window.

86
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Now you can choose the cup size according to the previous size preset.

87
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Just click the down arrow.

88
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Select the cup size you want to use.

89
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
The chest cup size will be adjusted accordingly.

90
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:32,000
You can see the value just set is displayed at the bottom of the chest size.

91
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:35,000
This function can help you create a more standard chest size.

92
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Make the virtual model chest adjustment process more standardized.

93
00:06:42,000 --> 00:07:06,519
Use the

94
00:07:06,519 --> 00:07:07,519
reset.

95
00:07:08,079 --> 00:07:08,680
first.

96
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:09,720
2.

97
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,000
to make a virtual model chest adjustment as usual.

